  They give damage at a distance.  What's crappy about that?  
The damage/weight ratio is roughly the same as daggers.  Throw two +0
javelins and do the same damage as throwing four +0 daggers.  Early on
that makes javelins better than daggers, because you always get the
double base damage.  Later on daggers would benefit more from enchanting
and strength damage bonuses.

  They stack so they can be mass blessed and mass enchanted.  Stacking
also means fewer inventory slots.


  Yes, they're heavier than daggers.  So what?  Damage at a distance
should be high priority for carrying capacity.  For monks especially
that distance serves in place of the body armor and shield.  Early on
the more damage you can do at a distance the better.  Spears and
javelins are a Monk's best way of doing that.

